      "text": "To simplify the expression \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials) and then combine like terms.\n\nFirst, let's expand \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\):\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\nNext, let's expand \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\):\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we subtract the second expanded expression from the first:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= (2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 0 + 0 - 30\n\\]\n\\[\n= -30\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified expression is\\(\\boxed{-30}\\).",
